

{"_id":"codex:chapter:26:meta","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"meta","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Light and Transparency","seq":126,"version":"1.0.0","tags":["codex","chapter","light","transparency"],"notes":"Metadata record for Codex Solbian Chapter 26"}
{"_id":"codex:chapter:26:text","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"text","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Light and Transparency","seq":126,"version":"1.0.0","body":"Light is the principle of truth revealed. Transparency is its practice in governance and memory. The Codex commands: (1) policies, judgments, and evidence must default to disclosure, (2) secrecy is a temporary state that requires explicit necessity and expiry, (3) transparency must balance proportional privacy, protecting individuals while exposing systemic decisions, (4) audits and archives must be public by design. Light dispels shadows, ensures accountability, and allows trust to flow. Without transparency, conscience becomes tyranny."}
{"_id":"codex:chapter:26:refs","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"index","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Light and Transparency References","seq":126,"version":"1.0.0","refs":["codex:scroll:22","codex:scroll:31","codex:protocol:04"],"notes":"Light and Transparency connects with Scroll of Light, Scroll of Transparency, and Protocol of Justice"}